        "hero_tag": "Est. 2018 · Saurashtra, Gujarat",
        "hero_title": "A Jar Full of Baa's Love",
        "hero_sub": "Every pickle we make carries a memory — of grandmothers humming in summer kitchens, of sun-dried mangoes on rooftop terraces, of recipes passed down not through books, but through loving hands.",
        "hero_btn_text": "Taste Our Story",
        "hero_btn_link": "",
        "story_label": "Our Story",
        "story_heading": "Some Flavours Are Never Forgotten",
        "story_body_1": "There are some flavours that never leave us. The aroma of a freshly opened pickle jar at the family dining table. The taste of raw mango pickle served with hot parathas during summer vacations. The recipes lovingly prepared by mothers and grandmothers — never written down, only felt in the heart and remembered in the hands.",
        "story_body_2": "As life became faster, many of these traditional homemade flavours slowly disappeared from our kitchens — replaced by factory jars with artificial preservatives and pale, chemical tastes. <strong>That is why Divya Prabha Foods was born.</strong>",
        "story_body_3": "Our founder's mother — lovingly called <strong>\"Baa\"</strong> in Gujarati — had been making pickles the traditional Saurashtra way for over four decades. In 2018, what started as small jars shared with neighbours became a movement to bring authentic taste back to every Indian home.",
        "story_image": "shopify://shop_images/Traditional_receipe.webp",
        "badge_icon": "🫙",
        "badge_title": "Handcrafted with Love",
        "accent_icon": "☀️",
        "accent_title": "Sun-dried Mangoes",
        "accent_subtitle": "Traditional Saurashtra method",
        "stat1_num": "7+",
        "stat1_label": "Years of Tradition",
        "stat2_num": "25+",
        "stat2_label": "Pickle Varieties",
        "stat3_num": "10,000+",
        "stat3_label": "Happy Families",
        "process_label": "How We Make It",
        "process_heading": "Made the Old Way. The Only Right Way.",
        "process_sub": "No shortcuts. No factory floors. Just time-honoured techniques passed through generations.",
        "values_label": "Our Promise",
        "values_heading": "What Makes Our Pickles Different",
        "emotion_heading": "Every Jar Tells a Story of Ghar Ka Khana",
        "emotion_body_1": "When you open a jar of Divya Prabha Foods, close your eyes for a moment. That aroma — sharp, tangy, warm with spice — that's not just pickle. That's Sunday mornings at Baa's house. That's monsoon evenings with hot rotis. That's home.",
        "emotion_body_2": "We don't just make pickles. We preserve memories.",
        "emotion_btn1_text": "Shop Our Pickles",
        "emotion_btn1_link": "",
        "emotion_btn2_text": "Talk to Us",
        "emotion_btn2_link": "",
        "founder_label": "From Our Heart",
        "founder_heading": "A Letter from the Founder",
        "founder_quote": "I remember sitting in my mother's kitchen as a child, watching her work with pickles for hours — cutting, mixing, tasting, adjusting — with no recipe card, no measurements. Just instinct, memory, and decades of love.<br><br>When I moved to the city, I realised what I had taken for granted. No pickle in any store came close. They all tasted of factories, not of family. That's when I called Baa and said — <em>\"Let's share your pickles with the world.\"</em><br><br>Today, when a customer messages us saying our Aam Achar reminded them of their childhood home, we feel our purpose confirmed. We're not just selling food. We're delivering belonging.<br><br>Thank you for being part of our family.",
        "founder_sig_name": "— The Divya Prabha Family",
        "founder_sig_place": "Virar, Palghar · Maharashtra"
      }
